    djr:kind djr:kind-prose ;
    djr:order 2 ;
    djr:text "---\n\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s031-7.1> a djr:Section ;
    djr:headingSnapshot "### 7.1 테스트 격리"@ko ;
    djr:inDocument <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#d/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md> ;
    djr:sectionNumber "7.1" ;
    djr:sectionOwner djr:owner-graph .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s031-7.1/b1> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s031-7.1> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-norm ;
    djr:order 1 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2195, djr:R-2196 ;
    djr:text "\n각각의 테스트는 서로 독립적이어야 하며, **실행 순서에서도 독립적**이어야 한다. 이를 달성하기 위한 구체적 전략은 **공유 상태 제거**이다. [xUnit Test Patterns]\n\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s031-7.1/b2> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s031-7.1> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-norm ;
    djr:order 2 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2197 ;
    djr:text "전역 공유 상태는 Erratic Test(불안정 테스트)의 근본 원인이다. pytest fixture를 사용하여 테스트별 독립적인 상태를 생성한다.\n\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s031-7.1/b3> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s031-7.1> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-code ;
    djr:order 3 ;
    djr:text "```python\n# === 나쁨: 공유 상태로 인한 불안정 ===\nshared_list = []  # 전역 공유 상태 -> 테스트 순서에 따라 결과 달라짐\n\ndef test_add_item_erratic():\n    shared_list.append(\"item\")\n    assert len(shared_list) == 1  # 다른 테스트가 먼저 실행되면 실패\n\n\n# === 좋음: 각 테스트에서 독립적인 상태 사용 ===\n@pytest.fixture\ndef fresh_list():\n    return []\n\ndef test_add_item_stable(fresh_list):\n    fresh_list.append(\"item\")\n    assert len(fresh_list) == 1  # 항상 성공\n```\n\n" .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s032-7.2> a djr:Section ;
    djr:headingSnapshot "### 7.2 AAA 패턴: Arrange-Act-Assert [Osherove]"@ko ;
    djr:inDocument <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#d/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md> ;
    djr:sectionNumber "7.2" ;
    djr:sectionOwner djr:owner-graph .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s032-7.2/b1> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s032-7.2> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-norm ;
    djr:order 1 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2198, djr:R-2199 ;
    djr:text "\n테스트의 최종 코드 구조는 AAA 패턴을 따른다. 사고 과정에서는 Assert First(단언 우선)로 목적부터 정하되, 최종 코드는 위에서 아래로 자연스럽게 읽히도록 정리한다.\n\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s032-7.2/b2> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s032-7.2> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-norm ;
    djr:order 2 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2200 ;
    djr:text "> Assert First 사고법 [테스트주도 개발]: 완료 시 통과해야 할 단언부터 머릿속에 떠올리고, \"이 값은 어디서 오는가?\" 를 역추적하며 필요한 설정을 도출한다.\n\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s032-7.2/b3> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s032-7.2> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-code ;
    djr:order 3 ;
    djr:text "```python\ndef test_transfer_funds():\n    # --- Arrange: 테스트에 필요한 객체와 상태를 준비한다 ---\n    source = Account(balance=5000)\n    target = Account(balance=1000)\n    service = TransferService()\n\n    # --- Act: 테스트 대상 행위를 실행한다 (단 하나만) ---\n    result = service.transfer(source, target, amount=2000)\n\n    # --- Assert: 기대 결과를 검증한다 ---\n    assert result.success is True\n    assert source.balance == 3000\n    assert target.balance == 3000\n```\n\n" .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s033-7.3> a djr:Section ;
    djr:headingSnapshot "### 7.3 테스트 데이터"@ko ;
    djr:inDocument <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#d/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md> ;
    djr:sectionNumber "7.3" ;
    djr:sectionOwner djr:owner-graph .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s033-7.3/b1> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s033-7.3> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-norm ;
    djr:order 1 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2201 ;
    djr:text "\n- 테스트를 읽을 때 쉽고 따라가기 좋을 만한 데이터를 사용하라\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s033-7.3/b2> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s033-7.3> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-norm ;
    djr:order 2 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2202 ;
    djr:text "- 데이터 간에 차이가 있다면 그 속에 **어떤 의미가 있어야** 한다\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s033-7.3/b3> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s033-7.3> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-norm ;
    djr:order 3 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2203 ;
    djr:text "- 동일한 상수를 여러 의미로 쓰지 마라 (예: `plus(2, 2)` 대신 `plus(2, 3)`)\n\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s034-7.4> a djr:Section ;
    djr:headingSnapshot "### 7.4 명백한 데이터"@ko ;
    djr:inDocument <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#d/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md> ;
    djr:sectionNumber "7.4" ;
    djr:sectionOwner djr:owner-graph .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s034-7.4/b1> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s034-7.4> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-norm ;
    djr:order 1 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2204 ;
    djr:text "\n테스트 자체에 예상되는 값과 실제 값을 포함하고, 이 둘 사이의 **관계를 드러내기 위해 노력**하라.\n\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s034-7.4/b2> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s034-7.4> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-code ;
    djr:order 2 ;
    djr:text "```python\n# 나쁨: 49.25가 왜 정답인지 알 수 없다\nassert exchange(100, \"USD\", \"GBP\") == 49.25\n\n# 좋음: 계산 과정이 드러난다\nassert exchange(100, \"USD\", \"GBP\") == 100 / 2 * (1 - 0.015)\n```\n\n" .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s035-7.5> a djr:Section ;
    djr:headingSnapshot "### 7.5 테스트 명명 규칙 [Osherove]"@ko ;
    djr:inDocument <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#d/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md> ;
    djr:sectionNumber "7.5" ;
    djr:sectionOwner djr:owner-graph .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s035-7.5/b1> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s035-7.5> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-code ;
    djr:order 1 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2205 ;
    djr:text "\n```\n[테스트 대상 단위]_[상태/조건]_[기대 행위]\n```\n\n" .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s035-7.5/b2> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s035-7.5> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-code ;
    djr:order 2 ;
    djr:text "```python\ndef test_divide__divisor_is_zero__raises_value_error():\n    \"\"\"divide 함수가 0으로 나눌 때 ValueError를 발생시킨다.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"0으로 나눌 수 없습니다\"):\n        divide(10, 0)\n\n\ndef test_withdraw__amount_exceeds_balance__returns_insufficient_funds():\n    \"\"\"출금액이 잔액을 초과하면 잔액 부족 오류를 반환한다.\"\"\"\n    account = Account(balance=1000)\n    result = account.withdraw(1500)\n    assert result.error == \"잔액 부족\"\n```\n\n" .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s036-7.6> a djr:Section ;
    djr:headingSnapshot "### 7.6 Mock보다 출력·상태 검증을 우선한다 [Khorikov]"@ko ;
    djr:inDocument <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#d/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md> ;
    djr:sectionNumber "7.6" ;
    djr:sectionOwner djr:owner-graph .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s036-7.6/b1> a djr:Block ;
    djr:inSection <https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s036-7.6> ;
    djr:kind djr:kind-norm ;
    djr:order 1 ;
    djr:statesNorm djr:R-2206, djr:R-2207, djr:R-2208, djr:R-2209 ;
    djr:text "\nTDD로 구현을 몰아갈 때 검증 방식은 **출력 기반 > 상태 기반 > 통신 기반(Mock)** 순으로 선호한다. Mock은 외부 의존성(DB, API, 파일시스템, 결제, 알림 등) 격리에만 쓰고, 핵심 로직은 실제 객체의 출력/상태로 검증한다. 이는 무엇을 어떻게 검증할지에 대한 실천 원칙이며, Mock 우선순위표와 구체적 사용법(`Mock(spec=)`, `side_effect`, 호출/순서 검증)은 작성법이므로 `implementation-test` §7을 따른다. Mock이 필요한 경계에서의 *도구*는 pytest-mock `mocker` 픽스처다(자동 teardown) — 고전 학파 기본(§3 실제 협력 객체)은 불변이고 *도구만* 격상한다(무엇을·얼마나 mock할지는 위 우선순위가 소유).\n\n"@ko .

<https://numchida.com/ns/djr#s/dddjango/skills/discipline-tdd/references/final.md/s037-7.7> a djr:Section ;
    djr:headingSnapshot "### 7.7 깨진 테스트 / 깨끗한 체크인 [테스트주도 개발]"@ko ;
